Slide 4: Pythonic Truthiness
Falsy values: False, None, 0, 0.0, '', [], (), {}
Truthy values: non-empty strings, non-zero numbers, populated containers

Slide 4: Loop Else Clause
for item in items:
  if target == item: break
else: print('Not found!')
Executes only if no break was encountered.

Slide 1: Dictionaries: Key-Value Stores
student = {'id': 101, 'name': 'Aisha', 'grade': 'A'}
Fast O(1) key lookups via internal hash tables.

Slide 3: Dictionary Iteration Patterns
for key, val in student.items():
    print(f'{key} -> {val}')

Slide 4: Sets & Set Theory
unique_ids = set([1, 2, 2, 3]) # {1, 2, 3}
Operators: | (union), & (intersection), - (difference)

Slide 1: OOP: Blueprints & Objects
class Student:
    def __init__(self, name, id):
        self.name = name
        self.id = id

Slide 4: Inheritance & super()
class GraduateStudent(Student):
    def __init__(self, name, id, thesis):
        super().__init__(name, id)
        self.thesis = thesis

Slide 1: Defensive Code: Try-Except
try:
    val = int(user_input)
except ValueError as e:
    print(f'Invalid input: {e}')

